1
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Crown for Christmas is a romance, tv movie film directed by Alex Zamm.

2
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Allie Foster, a struggling New York artist, reluctantly accepts to act as a
governess to a rebellious Princess Theodora of Winshire.

3
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
When Allie forms an unlikely bond with the princess, she attracts the attention of the handsome
King Maximillian, who’s facing an arranged marriage against his heart’s wishes.

4
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:30,000
As Christmas Eve draws near, Allie finds herself swept up in
romance, royalty and the spirit of the holidays.

5
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Allie Foster, played by Danica McKellar.

6
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Maximillian, played by Rupert Penry-Jones.

7
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:18,000
Theodora, played by Ellie Botterill.

8
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:54,000
Fergus, played by Pavel Douglas.

9
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Chancellor Riggs, played by Colin McFarlane.

10
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Miss Wick, played by Amy Marston.

11
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Crown for Christmas  is a 2015 American made-for-television romantic
comedy film starring Danica McKellar and Rupert Penry-Jones.

12
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
The film premiered on Hallmark Channel on November 27, 2015, as part of
their Countdown to Christmas seasonal programming block.

13
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
The film explores themes of princess, castle, royalty, king, governess.

14
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:30,000
The tone is emotional.
